##gff-version 3
#!gff-spec-version 1.21
#!processor fermdb tests/fixtures/genomics/protein_qc (synthetic)
##sequence-region NC_TEST01.1 1 1892
##sequence-region NC_TEST24.1 1 300
##sequence-region NC_TEST90.1 1 243
#
# The failure corpus. Nothing here is a mistake in the fixture: every locus is a named failure
# mode the gate has to report rather than crash on or wave through. The genome it is read against
# is the SAME mini.fna the clean corpus uses -- the errors are in this annotation and in
# mini.broken.faa, which is how a real phase or coordinate error arrives.
#
#   YTEST01W  CDS start moved one base 3' of the truth. The classic off-by-one; it frameshifts
#             the whole ORF.
#   YTEST02W  correct coordinates, but the second CDS segment declares phase 0 where its own
#             exon lengths say 1. The translation is still exact -- which is exactly why this
#             has to be counted and printed: an internally inconsistent phase is invisible in
#             the identity number.
#   YTEST03C  minus-strand CDS with its 5' end (the higher coordinate) moved one base.
#   YTEST04W  correct coordinates; mini.broken.faa holds a STALE record for it, differing at
#             one residue. This is the shape a protein FASTA from a superseded annotation
#             release has, and it is the only failure here that is not a coordinate fault.
#   YTEST05W  an in-frame stop codon in the middle of the CDS.
#   YTEST06W  one codon is NNN in the assembly; the protein record names the residue.
#   YTEST07W  annotated with protein_id=NP_TEST007.1, which mini.broken.faa does not contain.
#   YTEST09W  declares transl_table=11. fermdb.genetic_code implements 1 and 3; 11 is refused
#             by name rather than silently read as 1 (it differs from 1 only in start codons,
#             which is precisely why the silent version of this would never be noticed).
#   YTEST10W  a TGA the protein record reads through as selenocysteine (U).
#   YTEST08W  on NC_TEST90.1, whose region feature states no genome=. No table can be resolved,
#             so it is refused.
#   Q0TEST1   the mitochondrial ORF again, this time with NO transl_table attribute. It still
#             has to be read under table 3, via its sequence's region genome=mitochondrion.
#
# mini.broken.faa additionally holds NP_TESTORPHAN.1, a protein record no CDS in this file
# produces.
#
NC_TEST01.1	fermdb	region	1	1892	.	+	.	ID=NC_TEST01.1:1..1892;Name=NC_TEST01.1;gbkey=Src;genome=chromosome;mol_type=genomic DNA
###
NC_TEST24.1	fermdb	region	1	300	.	+	.	ID=NC_TEST24.1:1..300;Name=NC_TEST24.1;Is_circular=true;gbkey=Src;genome=mitochondrion;mol_type=genomic DNA
###
NC_TEST90.1	fermdb	region	1	243	.	+	.	ID=NC_TEST90.1:1..243;Name=NC_TEST90.1;gbkey=Src;mol_type=genomic DNA
###
